<PageLayout
  title="Privacy — what Billwright does and does not collect"
  description="Billwright runs entirely in your browser. No accounts, no analytics, no uploads and no third-party requests. Here is exactly what is stored and where."
  heading="Privacy"
  standfirst="Short version: your invoice never leaves your device, and there is nothing here to log you into."
>
  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing. There is no account system, no sign-up form, no analytics script and no tracking
    pixel. We do not have a server that receives what you type, so there is no copy of your invoice
    on our side to lose, sell or hand over.
  </p>

  <h2>What your browser stores</h2>
  <p>
    The generator and the calculators save what you have typed to your browser's local storage so
    the page is still filled in when you come back. That data stays on your device, is readable only
    by this site in this browser, and is never transmitted. Clearing your browser's site data removes
    it, and so does the "Start a new invoice" button.
  </p>

  <h2>Where the PDF is made</h2>
  <p>
    In the tab you are looking at. The PDF is assembled by JavaScript running on your machine and
    saved straight to your downloads folder. It is not generated on a server, so it is never
    transmitted anywhere.
  </p>

  <h2>Requests that leave your browser</h2>
  <p>
    Loading a page makes no third-party requests at all. The two fonts are served from this domain
    rather than from Google Fonts, so nobody else sees your IP address when a page loads.
  </p>

  <h2>The one exception: AI draft</h2>
  <p>
    The generator has an optional "Describe the work" box. If you type into it and press the button,
    that sentence — and nothing else — is sent to our server, which passes it to Anthropic's Claude
    API to turn into line items. It is the only feature on the site that makes a network request
    with anything you typed.
  </p>
  <p>
    What is <em>not</em> sent: your business name and address, your client, your invoice number, your
    dates, your existing line items, your totals and your notes. The amounts on the returned items
    are added up on your device as always.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you never open that box, nothing about your invoice is ever transmitted. Anthropic does not
    train models on API inputs; their retention terms apply to the sentence you send. Every other
    field in the generator stays local whether you use the feature or not.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising</h2>
  <p>
    This site is paid for by display advertising. Where ad slots are filled, the ad network involved
    sets its own terms and may use cookies; that relationship is between you and the network, and it
    never has access to what you typed into the generator.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
